+ * outside that lock overwrote an SPU commit landing between the read and the
+ * write, and the woken task slept forever (upstream #340, Twisted Metal's
+ * post-FX barrier). Do the whole read-modify-write under the lock, as a PPU
+ * atomic would, and drop every reservation on the line. Raw guest bytes:
+ * vm_write32 takes the lock-line lock itself and the lock does not nest. */
+static void spu_signalled_update(uint32_t taskset_ea, uint32_t taskId, int set)
+{
